/code-review high — loop R1, round 4 — range 7bb533f8..9024a1bd (branch 2026-10-08-mockups-served-at-a-url)

The review found 10 issues. The two most serious mean the link check can say "links OK" when links are actually broken.

- **How I checked:** I reviewed the 8 commits on the worktree branch (31f47d73..9024a1bd) plus the uncommitted plan `index.md`, and ran the three mockups test suites (36/36 pass).
- **Confirmed by running the scripts on a temp tree:** findings 1 and 3. With an orphaned `old-checkout/index.html`, a link to `/old-checkout` passed the check. With only `checkout/` on disk, links to `/Checkout` and `/CHECKOUT/` gave `LINKS OK`.
- **Docs (finding 10):** the stale site manual is already assigned to U5, which is still pending in wave 3. I list it only because the repo rule asks for docs in the same commit as the behaviour change.

